From 943e9ea4a85d1510169f058c78c7bcc3a70d7a5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:04:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: stm32_iwdg: Propagate errors from optional IRQ
 lookup

commit 553edb793e5be81a0d9bdb7b5aa2f9f1e0eb237b upstream

platform_get_irq_optional() returns a positive IRQ number on success or
a negative error code on failure. For an optional IRQ, -ENXIO indicates
that no IRQ is available, while other errors should be propagated.

Propagate errors such as -EPROBE_DEFER and -EINVAL instead of continuing
probe without the IRQ.

Signed-off-by: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260807080447.35479-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck <linux@roeck-us.net>
Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I9945821ae690799e3d21c3ee64f462cc08a8bc29
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/601442
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/watchdog/stm32_iwdg.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/watchdog/stm32_iwdg.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/stm32_iwdg.c
@@ -321,8 +321,11 @@ static int stm32_iwdg_irq_init(struct pl
 		return 0;
 
 	irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);
-	if (irq <= 0)
+	if (irq < 0) {
+		if (irq != -ENXIO)
+			return irq;
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	if (of_property_read_bool(np, "wakeup-source")) {
 		ret = devm_device_init_wakeup(dev);
